## Fastest way: the AutoSkill CLI

```bash
{{ ctx.companion_install_command }}   # once per machine (or: uv tool install autoskill-local)
autoskill login {{ ctx.server_url }}  # opens the browser to connect this machine
{% if ctx.manifest_url %}
autoskill {{ "trial install" if ctx.trial else "install" }} --from {{ ctx.manifest_url }} --target {{ adapter.id }}{% if ctx.trial %} --token <trial-token>{% endif %}
{% else %}
autoskill {{ "trial install" if ctx.trial else "install" }} {{ ctx.skill_name }}@{{ ctx.version }} --target {{ adapter.id }}
{% endif %}
```

The CLI downloads everything listed below, verifies the checksums, installs the shared components and the MCP
servers, copies the skill into the right folder, registers the MCP servers in `{{ adapter.mcp_config_path }}`,
asks you for the required environment values and stores them only in your agent's configuration.
